Quick Links|5-Year UV Warranty|Installation Guide & Video|Eco Plant Cleaner|Compare: Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel Designer Plants’ Premium Artificial Boxwood Roll at 3m x 1m delivers 3 square metres of UV-resistant boxwood foliage in a single flexible roll — engineered as a fast-coverage alternative to the rigid 1m x 1m panel format. The roll ships with a free integrated privacy backing layer, providing near-total visual blocking through the foliage when the roll is mounted to fences, frames, or vertical surfaces. The boxwood foliage is constructed from low-density polyethylene (LDPE) with integrated UVTex inhibitors — UV resistant for direct Australian sun and engineered to hold colour year-round across coastal, inland, and tropical climate zones. The flexible substrate cuts to size with standard scissors and conforms to curved or irregular mounting surfaces — making the roll the format of choice for fast event installations, balcony privacy applications, and any installation where rigid panels are impractical. A 3m x 1m roll covers a balcony divider in one piece. A bare timber fence in three. The format does what panels can’t — flexes around corners, cuts to size with scissors, and arrives with the privacy backing already attached. Specified for residential balconies, hospitality fit-outs, and event installations where speed of coverage matters as much as the finished look. Specifications    Dimensions 100 cm × 300 cm (3 m² coverage per roll)   Material LDPE boxwood foliage on a flexible mesh substrate   UV protection UVTex UV inhibitors integrated within the leaf — not surface-applied   Privacy backing Integrated free with every roll — near-total visual blocking   Indoor / Outdoor Suitable for both, including shaded outdoor positions   Installation Cut to size with scissors; attach to walls, fences, frames, or stands using cable ties or fixings   Maintenance No watering, pruning, or pest control required   Warranty 5-year UV warranty (view warranty terms)    Where the Premium Boxwood Roll Is Used 3 m² in one roll. Cuts to size, conforms to curves, ships with privacy backing already attached. These are the contexts in which the roll format is most often specified. Indoor walls, hallways, and reception areas. The roll format covers expanses that would require multiple panel-fixing operations. Especially effective on long hallway walls, reception backdrops, and feature walls where a continuous green expanse is the brief. Balconies, patios, and shaded garden fences. Apartment-balcony privacy is the single most common application — a 3m roll covers a typical balcony divider in one piece, with the integrated privacy backing eliminating the need for separate screening. Retail, hospitality, and office decor. Cafe and bar interiors, retail fit-outs, and corporate office breakout zones — the flexible roll handles curved walls, support columns, and irregular geometry that rigid panels cannot. Event backdrops, photo walls, and exhibitions. Wedding and event suppliers favour the roll format for fast install and pack-down. Cut-to-size flexibility allows custom backdrop dimensions without offcut waste. Pool surrounds and outdoor entertaining. Wraps timber-frame structures and pergola surrounds where a planted hedge would take seasons to establish. UV-resistant for direct sun. Photography and content creation. A flexible green backdrop that can be repositioned, rolled, and stored — without the rigid frame of panel-format greenery. Installation The flexible substrate cuts to size with standard scissors and conforms to curved or irregular surfaces. Attach using cable ties for grid-frame mounting, staples for timber substrates, or screws and washers for permanent wall installations. For step-by-step guidance, see the Installation Guide & Video. Why Designers and Commercial Operators Specify Designer Plants Designer Plants holds a 5-star rating across more than 20,000 verified customer reviews and has delivered commercial-grade installations for clients including BMW, Disney, Aperol, Facebook, Coca-Cola, Westfield, Virgin Australia, and VicRoads. A 5-year UV warranty is provided on all certified outdoor greenery panels. Designer Plants is Australia’s only artificial greenery supplier with a dedicated product recycling programme. Trade pricing and wholesale accounts are available. Contact the team on 1800 617 341 or at sales@designerplants.com.au to discuss project requirements. Care and Maintenance Dust the foliage with a soft brush for routine cleaning. For deeper cleaning, Designer Plants’ Eco Home Safe Artificial Plant Cleaner is safe for the LDPE foliage and substrate. No watering, pruning, or pest control is required. Frequently Asked Questions   Is the Premium Artificial Boxwood Roll suitable for outdoor use in Australia?  Yes. The boxwood foliage is constructed from LDPE with integrated UVTex UV inhibitors — engineered for direct Australian sun across all climate zones. The roll holds colour year-round and is backed by a 5-year UV warranty. View warranty terms.    How is the roll installed?  The flexible substrate cuts to size with standard scissors. Attach to walls, fences, frames, or event stands using cable ties (for grid-frame mounts), staples (for timber substrates), or screws and washers (for solid-wall installations). For full installation guidance, see the Installation Guide & Video.    How much area does one roll cover?  Each roll measures 100 cm by 300 cm — exactly 3 square metres of coverage. For larger projects, multiple rolls run end-to-end without visible joins when the cut edges are aligned and overlapped slightly.    What is included with the privacy backing?  Every roll ships with an integrated privacy backing layer at no extra charge. The backing provides near-total visual blocking through the foliage — eliminating the need for a separate screening layer behind the greenery for residential balcony or fence-line applications.    How does the roll compare to the Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel?  Both products use the same LDPE boxwood foliage with UVTex UV inhibitors. The roll format (100 × 300 cm flexible) suits fast coverage, curved surfaces, and cut-to-size applications. The Boxwood Hedge Screen Panel (1m × 1m) is the rigid format — better for permanent installations, joined panel walls, and fixed feature points.    Can the roll be used in commercial environments?  Yes. Specified across hospitality, retail, corporate, and event-industry installations. Trade and wholesale accounts are available — contact 1800 617 341 for project pricing on multi-roll orders.    Is the roll safe around children and animals?  Yes. The LDPE foliage and substrate contain no toxic substances. The roll has no sharp edges or fixings. Standard installation positions place the roll above pet height; for child-safe environments, ensure the mounting fixings are secure and concealed.    Is the boxwood roll recyclable?  Designer Plants is Australia’s only artificial greenery supplier with a dedicated product recycling programme. End-of-life rolls can be returned to Designer Plants for processing rather than landfill — contact 1800 617 341 for recycling-programme details.    What maintenance does the boxwood roll require?  No watering, pruning, or pest control is required. For routine cleaning, dust the foliage with a soft brush or use Designer Plants’ Eco Home Safe Artificial Plant Cleaner for deeper cleaning.    How is the roll shipped?  Ships rolled from the Designer Plants Melbourne warehouse with door-to-door tracking, Australia-wide. The roll format is significantly lighter and more compact than equivalent panel coverage — making it the cost-effective shipping option for large-area installations.    How long is the warranty on the boxwood roll?  A 5-year UV warranty applies to the foliage when used in standard outdoor and indoor conditions. View full warranty terms.    
